 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (the left-hand panel of the three-panel '68r' canvas, with one crop). Under a few lines of text there is a sun at the top, a round face ringed by flame-like rays with three short words inside its circle; a moon at the bottom, a face inside a blue and yellow crescent with a ring of text around it; and between them twenty-nine scattered stars, each with a short label beside it (to its right, except one near the lower left whose label is on its left). Eight stars have a small ring at the centre, two a dark dot, four are drawn in outline with little or no yellow, and one near the middle is larger than the rest. The transcription has twenty-nine star-unit label lines (f68r1.8 to f68r1.36), which matches my count of stars. Their order is not known to me: I numbered the stars from top to bottom (left to right where two are level) and paired the label lines in that order, which is an assumption made from the line ids alone, so the star-to-label pairing may be wrong for any star and should not be relied on without a check against the label positions. The sun and moon are not paired with a label line.",
